<title>UK: ICI up as Merrill repeats positive stance.</title>
<headline>ICI up as Merrill repeats positive stance.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-05-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Imperial Chemical Industries Plc rose to a five-month high on Tuesday as Merrill Lynch analysts repeated an &quot;accumulate&quot; rating and a 900p valuation on the stock, dealers said.  </p>
<p>The stock was up 10-1/2p at 797-1/2 by 0934 GMT, some  14 percent above its level at the start of May before it was boosted by last week's $8 billion acquisition of Unilever Plc's speciality chemicals arm.</p>
<p>A report in Tuesday's Financial Times said the stock had also been boosted by an upgrade by HSBC James Capel. Market sources said the move, to &quot;hold&quot; from &quot;sell,&quot; had been made at the end of last week.</p>
<p>-- David Holmes, London Newsroom +44 171 542 4367</p>
